# Python processing

- Keep processors pure: no FastAPI, request, response, filesystem, or UI imports.
- State BGR/RGB/grayscale, dtype, range, alpha policy, and border behavior in each public operation.
- Validate parameters at a defined boundary; do not silently correct invalid kernels or thresholds.
- Avoid in-place mutation of the supplied image unless the function contract says so.
- Timing measures the operation only, excluding image decode/encode and HTTP work.
- Floating calculations use an explicit scale; clipping and integer conversion happen at named output boundaries.
- Add invariant-based tests using deterministic synthetic fixtures before optimizing.
